stion/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $z$-axis. So, the $i$ and $j$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=i,\\,G(x,y,z)=-j\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *negative* $z$-direction, so the $k$ component of our vector field is negative. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=k\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $k$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}\\,k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122670/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "888aa30d-7179-507c-a30c-38209587333b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122670"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123750/selection/b33a9110bb3e6bc1e0a51e01fefd7e3ccf781463a0e13e3c47241b2f1b341226" :answer/id #uuid "8e5ce636-0258-5495-8056-6a9fc8b574d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "H(x,y,z)=-\\,i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123750/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "158c228f-5bf9-5767-afa0-73f0d5609088" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123750/selection/8bb04d13666657a38749bb45c4b97e75e0340e0439c9d1cfc6f9269743e40932" :answer/id #uuid "a8e1b7d1-9d13-5d64-af17-ee141dcf9ef3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "G(x,y,z)=i-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123750/selection/13a7778946ad7880fdc216cb48de7a88a7e8a0632db645871096112f80627933" :answer/id #uuid "2a59f5d2-c9c3-5cf7-8207-21fe2dc86727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :a