 we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=-{e}^{y}\\,k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123750/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "888aa30d-7179-507c-a30c-38209587333b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123750"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
